- Save `curr.next` before you overwrite it, or you lose the rest of the list.
- Return `prev`, not `curr`. At loop exit `curr` is `null`.
- The old head ends up as the tail with `next = null`, which happens automatically because `prev` starts as `null`.
- Empty and single-node lists work without special cases.

A recursive version is also possible, but it uses O(n) stack and can overflow on long lists, so prefer the iterative one.

